* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    deffun voc_guard(f) calling '!voc_guard'
*    if not(voc_guard(file.var)) then stop
*
* Owner's rulings 12 and 14 (Solo for Windows, 25 Sep 2026): a DIRECT edit of
* the VOC needs the administrator password (ADMIN).  op_dio3.c refuses a user
* program's own write, delete or clear of a VOC in C; the verbs that edit a
* file the user names (ED, EDIT, COPY, COPYP, DELETE, CLEAR.FILE, and
* DELETE.FILE and RENAME when the VOC itself is the target) are $internal,
* which the C test lets through, so they ask this instead.
*
* IT LOOKS AT THE FILE THAT WAS OPENED, NOT AT THE NAME THAT WAS TYPED, so a
* Q-pointer to a VOC, or "voc" in any case, is caught.  A VOC is a DH (dynamic)
* file whose last path component is "voc" - the same rule as
* voc_write_refused() in C.  The dictionary, voc.dic, is not the VOC.
*
* Returns @true when the edit may go ahead: not a VOC, or ADMIN is on.  On
* @false it has already said why (11008).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function voc_guard(f)
$catalog !voc_guard

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   p = downcase(fileinfo(f, FL$PATH))
   if p[len(p), 1] = '/' then p = p[1, len(p) - 1]
   last = field(p, '/', dcount(p, '/'))

*  30 Sep 26 LSOLO 12 - RULING 33 (Windows Solo): SDSYS's gcat, global.bp.out and
*  solo.policy (ruling 34's deny list) are the SD Core server's, changed only
*  by a session signed in with the global password - ADMIN is NOT enough, so
*  this comes before the ADMIN test.  The C gate (op_dio3.c
*  global_write_refused) lets $internal verbs through, and COPY, ED, DELETE and
*  the rest are $internal.  On Linux the SDSYS directory IS the install's home
*  directory (no "sdsys" component), so the test is the full path: @SDSYS plus
*  the name.  A symbolic link to one of them is NOT recognised here - the
*  tree belongs to the Linux user, so this governs what SD will do, not what
*  that user can do to the files from outside SD (op_dio3.c says the same).
   if fileinfo(f, FL$TYPE) = FL$TYPE.DIR then
      sd.dir = downcase(@sdsys)
      if sd.dir[len(sd.dir), 1] = '/' then sd.dir = sd.dir[1, len(sd.dir) - 1]
      if p = sd.dir : '/gcat' or p = sd.dir : '/global.bp.out' or p = sd.dir : '/solo.policy' then
         if kernel(K$GLOBAL.SESSION, -1) then return @true
         display sysmsg(11028) ;* The global catalogue can only be changed by the SD Core server
         return @false
      end
   end

   if kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1) then return @true

   if fileinfo(f, FL$TYPE) # FL$TYPE.DH then return @true

   if last # 'voc' then return @true

   display sysmsg(11008) ;* The VOC can only be changed after ADMIN
   return @false
end

* END-CODE
